// The approval gate written against the DENIAL itself.
//
// Nobody should write this -- it grants the trade precisely when the approval failed. It is here
// to establish the other half of the claim in approval_gate_response.dw.
//
// Without it, "the response gate stays shut on a denied approval" is consistent with a duller
// explanation: that `error` events are somehow invisible to temporal matching. This file rules
// that out. `error` is an ordinary author-defined event kind and a policy matches it if it says
// so, which makes the response-gate result a fact about AgentCore's RECORDING convention rather
// than about the Dogwood engine.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1000s Anchor::Action::"Approve"::error{ }
};
